{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch25VPTfjmsSqq2tVREpr", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I'm not signing off. I found one grouping-direction bug that I reproduced three times, but the developer could not reproduce it from my steps, so it is still open.\n\n**Covered and working**\n- **Sort sheet:** The grouping direction toggle flips correctly, and the setting survives closing and reopening the sheet. Grouping by due date in ascending order shows Thursday, Nov 24, Dec 4, then No due date, which is the correct order.\n- **Task search:** Results update as text is typed (`2 lit` filters to Buy milk). Notes are searched (`example` finds Read docs). A subtask shows under its parent when the parent matches. A no-match query shows the empty state. Clearing the query restores the full list.\n- **Repeat picker:** Custom recurrence opens with the weekday row ordered Sun to Sat, which matches the en-US locale the device appears to use. Selecting Mon and Fri saves as \"Repeats weekly on Mon, Fri\" and persists after leaving and reopening the editor. Completing Pay rent moves it to Monday, Dec 7, which is the next selected weekday.\n\n**Open issue (reproduced 3 times; developer could not reproduce)**\n- Set Grouping to \"By due date\" with direction Descending. Close and reopen the sheet and it still shows Descending.\n- Choose \"By start date\" and then \"By due date\" again. The row now shows Ascending.\n- This also happens when switching through \"By priority\". Each time, the saved direction is replaced by a fixed default for the group.\n- The developer's reply to the report was \"could not reproduce with the steps given.\" The steps are in the report I filed. Please ask the developer to check whether re-selecting a group is supposed to ignore the saved direction.\n\n**Not verified**\n- I could not confirm that the weekday order follows the device's first-day-of-week setting beyond the en-US-style display.\n- Landscape rotation with the search field and keyboard open rendered badly and did not recover on its own. I rotated back to portrait. I did not file it because I could not reproduce it cleanly.\n\n**Data I changed while testing**\n- Pay rent now repeats weekly on Mon and Fri, not monthly, and its due date moved from Dec 4 to Dec 7.\n- Grouping is back to \"By due date\" with Descending, as it started.\n\nI can revert Pay rent to monthly on Dec 4 if you want the seed data restored."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2493, "cache_read_input_tokens": 284916, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 2493}, "output_tokens": 4, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "340d5be7-3fc6-4d5e-95ad-43a03b596be2", "uuid": "3e986853-44a5-4f2b-831f-3e452ef9be6f", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T03:03:54.910Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch25VPAonhKyokSgNp4Gc"}
